      "content": "For those exhibiting mischievous or deliberately disruptive behavior, deflection and maintaining professional neutrality are key strategies. Do not engage in power struggles or attempt to \"win\" an argument, as this fuels the chaos. A simple, neutral response like, \"I need to focus on helping you feel better right now,\" while consistently repeating safety rules, can interrupt the dynamic. Routinely checking in with compassionate but firm statements helps anchor the interaction back to patient care.",
